Band Visual & Press Photoshoot Prompt: A triptych shot in the central atrium of a derelict, sun-drenched mall. In the foreground, 'The Resonator' – a heavily scarred upright bass wrapped in flickering neon tape – leans against a water-damaged F.A.O. Schwarz sign. In the midground, Coda, obscured by the diffuse, dusty light filtering through a skylight, stands amidst a tangle of live wires, wearing a tattered prom dress emblazoned with glowing circuit patterns, hand reaching out to a console that sparks faintly. In the background, Jolt's silhouette is visible behind a graffiti-covered arcade machine, his cloak emitting faint green static, holding a makeshift percussion device made from a broken 'Space Invaders' screen. The air shimmers with heat haze and fine dust motes, catching the last golden hour light, suggesting both apocalypse and strange rebirth.

Descriptive Mood or Vibe: Melancholic digital aggression, romantic despair amidst industrial ruins, desperate beauty in decay.

